      "question_text": "Lipids are an important part of the human diet.\n \n(a) \nFatty acids react with glycerol to form fats and oils. State the name of the chemical link \nformed in this reaction and the name of the other product.\n[1]\n \nName of the chemical link:\n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n \nName of the other product:\n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n(b) \nThe table below shows average figures for the percentage fatty acid composition of \nsome common fats and oils.\nSource of fat \nor oil\n% saturated \nfatty acids \n(total)\n% monounsaturated \nfatty acid oleic\n% polyunsaturated fatty acids\nlinoleic\nlinolenic\nBeef fat\n59\n38\n3\n-\nCoconut oil\n90\n8\n2\n-\nCorn oil\n25\n26\n47\n2\nCotton seed oil\n22\n35\n43\n-\nOlive oil\n15\n78\n7\n-\nSoybean oil\n14\n28\n50\n8\n \n \n(i) \nDeduce, with a reason, which fat or oil from the table above has the lowest \niodine number.\n[1]\n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n \n(ii) \nDeduce, with a reason, which fat or oil from the table above is most likely to \nbecome rancid when exposed to the air.\n[1]\n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .